>
> How much does that influence the total numbers?

Probably more than anything else I mentioned.  Monsters receive a
rnd_defensive_item with probability m_lev/50, if they meet the
precondition that they are not animals, not mindless, don't have an
exploding attack, and are not S_GHOST or S_KOP.  Approximately 1/3 of
rnd_defensive_items are potions of *healing.  (Between 3/8 and 3/11
depending on monster difficulty, slightly more on no-teleport levels.)

(I should note the special case of soldiers, of whom 12/13 don't even
get a check for defensive/misc magic items, presumably to avoid making
barracks into treasure hoards of these sorts of items.)

Early in the game, this probably doesn't matter much, but when you're
seeing things like Dlvl20 throne rooms, I expect the effect is quite
significant.  (All monsters generated in a throne room are eligible
for rnd_*_items)

For example: if the average monster level currently being generated is
15, about 1/10 of eligible monsters will have a potion of *healing.

Player habits influencing numbers of monsters generated will
definitely have an effect here.

(Aside: it occurs to me that judicious use of create monster on
certain Quests could result in a whole bunch of assorted potions and
wands, including a good haul of potions of *healing; I can't say if it
would be worth it)

>> nymphs may have a potion of object detection (50%)
>
> Yes.  And for those I presume that they appear far more often than their
